.TH git-graft 1  "git-graft 0.2.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
git\-graft \- Run many coding agents on one repository without filling your disk. A faster, lighter replacement for git worktree.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit\-graft\fR [\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run many coding agents on one repository without filling your disk. A faster, lighter replacement for git worktree.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<REPO>\fR [default: .]
Repository checkout (or a subdirectory of it) whose grafts to manage
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print compact JSON (the default is indented JSON)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH OVERVIEW
.nf
Workflow:
  git graft add fix\-parser                               Create a graft; prints its path and lease
  cd ../<repo>.graft/fix\-parser                          Edit, test and commit with ordinary Git
  git graft merge fix\-parser \-\-lease <lease>             Merge into main and archive the graft
  git graft push fix\-parser \-\-lease <lease>              Or push its commits to origin for a pull request
  git graft restore fix\-parser \-\-lease <recovery_lease>  Reopen an archived graft

Leases:
  `add` returns a lease, a secret that proves the graft is yours. Commands that
  change a graft need it, through \-\-lease or the GIT_GRAFT_LEASE environment
  variable. Archiving returns a recovery_lease; `restore` takes it and returns a
  new lease. Keep leases out of logs.

Output:
  Every command prints JSON. A failure exits non\-zero and prints a JSON error
  whose "code" field names the problem, such as unmerged_work or workspace_busy.

Run `git graft <command> \-\-help` for a command\(aqs options and examples.
.fi
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBmcp\fR
Serve grafts to agents over MCP on stdin/stdout
.TP
\fBadd\fR
Create a graft: a lightweight, independent copy of the repository
.TP
\fBlist\fR
List active and recoverable grafts
.TP
\fBlocal\-files\fR
List the checkout's untracked and ignored files, which add \-\-include can copy
.TP
\fBstatus\fR
Show a graft's HEAD and changed files, or its environment with \-\-env
.TP
\fBdoctor\fR
Check Git support and whether grafts can share files
.TP
\fBexec\fR
Run a program inside a graft
.TP
\fBdeps\fR
Install and reuse dependencies
.TP
\fBhook\fR
Show the hooks and remotes .graftconfig and .graftconfig.local define, and trust them
.TP
\fBmerge\fR
Merge a graft's commits into a local branch, then archive the graft
.TP
\fBpush\fR
Push a graft's commits to a branch on a remote of the primary repository
.TP
\fBremove\fR
Archive a graft and its files. Refuses if it has unmerged work unless \-\-discard is given
.TP
\fBprune\fR
Archive every expired graft. Previews unless \-\-apply is given
.TP
\fBrestore\fR
Reopen an archived graft
.TP
\fBlock\fR
Protect a graft from moves, pruning and cleanup
.TP
\fBunlock\fR
Release a graft's lock
.TP
\fBmove\fR
Move a graft to another path on the same volume
.TP
\fBrepair\fR
Reconnect a graft that was moved outside git graft
.TP
\fBturn\fR
Take turns on something the grafts share, such as a development server or database
.PP
Run \fBgit graft\fR \fICOMMAND\fR \fB\-\-help\fR for a command's options and examples.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgit\-worktree\fR(1), https://github.com/mprync/git\-graft
